    <preface>
      <p>Restoring Territory Rights Act 2022</p>
      <p>No. 95, 2022</p>
      <p>An Act to amend the law in relation to the legislative powers of territories, and for related purposes</p>
      <p>Contents</p>
      <p>1	Short title	1</p>
      <p>2	Commencement	2</p>
      <p>3	Schedules	2</p>
      <p>Schedule 1—Amendments	3</p>
      <p><ref href="#part-1">Part 1</ref>—Amendments	3</p>
      <p>Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988	3</p>
      <p>Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978	3</p>
      <p><ref href="#part-2">Part 2</ref>—Application	4</p>
      <p>Restoring Territory Rights Act 2022</p>
      <p>No. 95, 2022</p>
      <p>An Act to amend the law in relation to the legislative powers of territories, and for related purposes</p>
      <p>[<i>Assented to 13 December 2022</i>]</p>
      <formula name="enacting">
        <p>The Parliament of Australia enacts:</p>
      </formula>
    </preface>
    <body>
      <section eId="sec-1">
        <num>1</num>
        <heading>Short title</heading>
        <content>
          <p>		This Act is the <i>Restoring Territory Rights Act 2022</i>.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-2">
        <num>2</num>
        <heading>Commencement</heading>
        <subsection eId="sec-2__subsec-1">
          <num>1</num>
          <content>
            <p>Each provision of this Act specified in column 1 of the table commences, or is taken to have commenced, in accordance with column 2 of the table. Any other statement in column 2 has effect according to its terms.</p>
          </content>
          <table>
            <tr>
              <th>Commencement information</th>
              <th>Commencement information</th>
              <th>Commencement information</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Column 1</td>
              <td>Column 2</td>
              <td>Column 3</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Provisions</td>
              <td>Commencement</td>
              <td>Date/Details</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>1.  The whole of this Act</td>
              <td>The day this Act receives the Royal Assent.</td>
              <td>13 December 2022</td>
            </tr>
          </table>
          <authorialNote placement="end" eId="note-1" marker="1">
            <content>
              <p>Note:	This table relates only to the provisions of this Act as originally enacted. It will not be amended to deal with any later amendments of this Act.</p>
            </content>
          </authorialNote>
        </subsection>
        <subsection eId="sec-2__subsec-2">
          <num>2</num>
          <content>
            <p>Any information in column 3 of the table is not part of this Act. Information may be inserted in this column, or information in it may be edited, in any published version of this Act.</p>
          </content>
        </subsection>
      </section>
      <section eId="sec-3">
        <num>3</num>
        <heading>Schedules</heading>
        <content>
          <p>Legislation that is specified in a Schedule to this Act is amended or repealed as set out in the applicable items in the Schedule concerned, and any other item in a Schedule to this Act has effect according to its terms.</p>
        </content>
      </section>
    </body>
    <attachments>
      <attachment>
        <hcontainer name="schedule" eId="schedule-1">
          <num>1</num>
          <heading>Amendments</heading>
          <hcontainer name="part" eId="schedule-1__part-1">
            <num>1</num>
            <heading>Amendments</heading>
            <hcontainer name="amendedAct" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-1">
              <heading>Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988</heading>
              <hcontainer name="item" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-1__item-1">
                <num>1</num>
                <heading>Subsections 23(1A) and (1B)</heading>
                <content>
                  <p>Repeal the subsections.</p>
                </content>
              </hcontainer>
            </hcontainer>
            <hcontainer name="amendedAct" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-2">
              <heading>Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978</heading>
              <hcontainer name="item" eId="schedule-1__part-1__amdact-2__item-1">
                <num>2</num>
                <heading>Section 50A</heading>
                <content>
                  <p>Repeal the section.</p>
                </content>
              </hcontainer>
            </hcontainer>
          </hcontainer>
          <hcontainer name="part" eId="schedule-1__part-2">
            <num>2</num>
            <heading>Application</heading>
            <hcontainer name="clause" eId="schedule-1__part-2__clause-3">
              <num>3</num>
              <heading>Application</heading>
              <hcontainer name="subclause" eId="schedule-1__part-2__clause-3__subclause-1">
                <num>1</num>
                <content>
                  <p>(1)	Despite the amendments made by this Schedule, the <i>Rights of the Terminally Ill Act</i><i> 1995</i> of the Northern Territory:</p>
                </content>
              </hcontainer>
              <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-2__clause-3__para-a">
                <num>a</num>
                <content>
                  <p>continues to have effect as a law of the Territory in relation to any act or thing that was done before <date date="1997-03-27">27 March 1997</date>; but</p>
                </content>
              </paragraph>
              <paragraph eId="schedule-1__part-2__clause-3__para-b">
                <num>b</num>
                <content>
                  <p>has no force or effect as a law of the Territory in relation to any act or thing done on or after that day.</p>
                </content>
              </paragraph>
              <hcontainer name="subclause" eId="schedule-1__part-2__clause-3__subclause-2">
                <num>2</num>
                <content>
                  <p>Subitem (1) applies subject to a contrary intention in a law of the Northern Territory that is enacted after the commencement of this item.</p>
                </content>
              </hcontainer>
              <content>
                <p>[<i>Minister’s second reading speech made in—</i></p>
                <p><i>House of Representatives on 1 August 2022</i></p>
                <p><i>Senate on 3 August 2022</i>]</p>
                <p>(67/22)</p>
              </content>
            </hcontainer>
          </hcontainer>
        </hcontainer>
